cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Verifile — Evidence-First SEC Filing Change Analysis
message: >-
  If you reference or reuse this work, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Du
    given-names: Yao
    alias: yaoDu
repository-code: https://github.com/yaoDu/verifile
url: https://github.com/yaoDu/verifile
abstract: >-
  A working prototype for fundamental equity research that compares a company's
  two most recent comparable SEC filings. All financial arithmetic is performed
  deterministically in Python from XBRL facts with auditable provenance; matched
  earlier and later evidence is retrieved for every claimed change; and any
  language-model contribution is constrained by schema, citation, numeric
  grounding and no-recommendation gates before it can be displayed. Research
  aid only, not investment advice.
keywords:
  - SEC EDGAR
  - XBRL
  - equity research
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - evidence-based AI
  - provenance
